e":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T17:07:01-07:00","id":887642,"title":"","content":"Start a website. Ask for prayers. Have some chat sessions. Record some inspirational videos. (File for tax exempt status).<br /> <br /> Done. Now you have your cult. Potentially a very LARGE one, pretty fast, depending on your web acumen and/or relevant divine powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-10T17:16:27-07:00","id":887656,"title":"","content":"is it true that having a too-large Cult can risk fatebind you in negative ways?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T12:58:16-07:00","id":888475,"title":"","content":"What differentiates a cult from a similar group of followers? I suspect that the Cult Birthright is going to have something to do with Legend while Followers will still be the dudes to order around, but I'm interested in knowing how they differ (if only because I have plans for a Scion of Hades with a Followers birthright to represent a variety of low-level functionaries).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T13:54:37-07:00","id":888530,"title":"","content":"or maybe another thing, should the ornateness and geometry of ones place of worship matter<br /> <br /> a real life note, I've been wishing deep down, that the gods whos temples and artifacts isis has been destroying, were real. is that weird?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-11T17:01:26-07:00","id":888663,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/772621-request-for-2nd-edition-give-the-gods-some-kind-of-cult-birthright?p=888530#post888530\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">or maybe another thing, should the ornateness and geometry of ones place of worship matter<br /> <br /> a real life note, I've been wishing deep down, that the gods whos temples and artifacts isis has been destroying, were real. is that weird?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I don't know which part of this would make me giggle like a psychotic child more. Watching The Islamic State [I want to slap whoever dubbed them Isis], getting destroyed by the gods in horrific and possibly humorous ways. <br /> <br /> Or watching the whole of the Judaism, Christianity, and Islam shit themselves as the realize that these gods who are an affront to their belief system, wreck shop and prove their existence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'll be your Huckleberry","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2397-the-dude","name":"The Dude","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T06:12:45-07:00","id":889040,"title":"","content":"hmmmn ideas on how it could be humorous?<br /> <br /> Hmmmn, say some epic social attributes, to get them killing each other?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T11:11:33-07:00","id":889248,"title":"","content":"I feel like this could be a balance problem, because then you run into issues of either A) worshippers don't give you power or B) worshippers do give you power and, with their ~1 billion active worshippers--far more than other pantheons have had in their entire history--the Devas are ludicrously overpowered.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Games are a way for us to explore what it means to be human, or inhuman, as the case may be. Let's all have a good time playing them.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/400-guitarsniper","name":"guitarsniper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-12T12:59:31-07:00","id":889306,"title":"","content":"This could be mitigated by having a maximum number of personal devout worshipers that any god could attain..eg. the same numbers you have in Followers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/333-achilles","name":"Achilles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar333_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-13T08:04:43-07:00","id":889899,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Dude</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or watching the whole of the Judaism, Christianity, and Islam shit themselves as the realize that these gods who are an affront to their belief system, wreck shop and prove their existence.</div> </div> </div> </div>The issue of monotheism is addressed, though not in a way that really dismisses the religions. I'm not gonna leave my boy Abraham in the lurch.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>guitarsniper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/772621-request-for-2nd-edition-give-the-gods-some-kind-of-cult-birthright?p=889248#post889248\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like this could be a balance problem, because then you run into issues of either A) worshippers don't give you power or B) worshippers do give you power and, with their ~1 billion active worshippers--far more than other pantheons have had in their entire history--the Devas are ludicrously overpowered.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've been thinking about this for a while. I've also considered that the Devas have a sort of American military-industrial complex going on; they have a large number of committed Terra Incognita, lots of powerful enemies, massive divine superweapons to maintain. If faith does provide some sort of power boost, it's possible they <i>need </i>that amount. It also commits them to a level of intervention and Fatebinding that might be distasteful.<br /> <br /> And just because the World is in a status quo at the moment doesn't mean the other pantheons will be satisfied with their number of worshippers.<br /> <br /> It's also possible that there are benefits other than a direct power boost, like having a pool to discharge power or bad Fatebindings or something. <i>Gods &amp; Monsters </i>for Fate Core had a variant on this system, where having a lot of shrines and worshippers basically meant having a massive power pool - but you still had to fill it. This is probably my preferred way of handling the Deva issue - they've got <i>much </i>bigger batteries than everyone else, but you're all pulling juice from the same shitty iPhone charger.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Neall Raemonn Price</span><br /> Beleaguered Scion Developer</b>","edited":{"userid":137,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","user":"Neall","date":". 05-13-2016, 11:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/137-neall","name":"Neall","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar137_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1204"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-14T12:46:12-07:00","id":890721,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/772621-request-for-2nd-edition-give-the-gods-some-kind-of-cult-birthright?p=889899#post889899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And just because the World is in a status quo at the moment doesn't mean the other pantheons will be satisfied with their number of worshippers.</div> </div> </div> </div>The worry I have here is that it would mean that games would have to operate on the timescale of demographic shifts, which, it would seem, requires either a lot of downtime or a truly long-term storyteller vision, because if the Old Gods are suddenly revealed to the world, it would make the most sense for people to revert to worshipping the deities of the ancestors--I don't see massive shrines of Amaterasu in Oslo, when Odin is there too--meaning that you're still looking at potential balance issues, especially for pantheons with relatively small population bases in the modern world.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neall</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/772621-request-for-2nd-edition-give-the-gods-some-kind-of-cult-birthright?p=889899#post889899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's also possible that there are benefits other than a direct power boost, like having a pool to discharge power or bad Fatebindings or something. <i>Gods &amp; Monsters </i>for Fate Core had a variant on this system, where having a lot of shrines and worshippers basically meant having a massive power pool - but you still had to fill it. This is probably my preferred way of handling the Deva issue - they've got <i>much </i>bigger batteries than everyone else, but you're all pulling juice from the same shitty iPhone charger.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a really clever solution.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Games are a way for us to explore what it means to be human, or inhuman, as the case may be. Let's all have a good time playing them.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/400-guitarsniper","name":"guitarsniper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}